  "headline_sentence": "Holding N_train exactly constant, the design does NOT dissociate rate from count at this sample size: the four candidate models are within 2.7 AIC of one another and the nominal winner leads by only 0.4 (best model by AIC: count_only_log_n, delta AIC to next 0.4; partial R2 log(count) 0.059 versus rate 0.043), which is below the delta-AIC 2 needed to prefer either. 0/5 equal-count contrasts and 0/12 equal-rate contrasts differing at p<0.05, largest equal-count difference 0.083 against a pre-registered 0.15 for dissociation and 0.05 for 'both matter weakly'. The pre-agreed reading is 'both matter weakly'; report it as a bound on what 3 seeds x 3 cell scales can resolve, not as a dissociation.",
